d be okay.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 26 and 76 is \\boxed{1976}.\n\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 26 and 76?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet\'s think step by step. 76 has two digits, so we can reason in two steps.\n1. Multiply 26 by the ones place digit 6 of 76: \\(26 \\times 6 = 156\\)\n2. Multiply 26 by the tens place digit 70 of 76: \\(26 \\times 70 = 1820\\)\n\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: \\(156 + 1820 = 1976\\).\nSo, the final computed product is 1976.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 26 and 76 is \\boxed{1976}.', '']  7%|7         | 36/500 [21:12<4:34:07, 35.45s/it]
