er mistakes here. \n\nDouble-checking 83*9:\n\n80*9 = 720, 3*9=27. 720+27=747. Correct.\n\n83*50: 83*5 is 415, so 415*10=4150. Correct.\n\nAdding 747 +4150:\n\n747 + 4000 = 4747, then +150 gives 4897. Correct.\n\nOkay, that seems accurate. So the answer is 4897.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 83 and 59?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 59 has two digits, so that we can reason in two steps.\n1. Multiply 83 by the ones place digit 9 of 59:  \n   \\(83 \\times 9 = 747\\).  \n2. Multiply 83 by the tens place digit 50 of 59:  \n   \\(83 \\times 50 = 4,\\!150\\).  \n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\(747 + 4,\\!150 = 4,\\!897\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{4897}.",
