ed one position left.\n\n9\u00d78=72, write down 2, carryover 7.\n\n5\u00d78=40 +7=47. So this partial product is 4720 (because of the shift).\n\nAdding 236 + 4720:\n\n236\n\n+4720\n\n=4956.\n\nYes, that's consistent. So the correct answer is definitely 4956. My initial confusion was because I was trying a different breakdown and miscalculating somewhere, but going back to the standard method clarifies it. So the key takeaway is to ensure each step accounts for place value properly and to verify with an alternative method if unsure.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 59 and 84 is \\boxed{4956}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 59 and 84, we can use the standard multiplication method by breaking down the numbers into their place values and then summing the results.\n\n1. **Multiply 59 by the ones place digit (4) of 84:**\n   \\[\n   59 \\times 4 = 236\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 59 by the tens place digit (80) of 84:**\n   \\[\n   59 \\times 80 = 4720\n   \\]\n\n3. **Sum the results of the two partial products:**\n   \\[\n   236 + 4720 = 4956\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 59 and 84 is \\(\\boxed{4956}\\).",
