ropriately. Summing them gives the correct result. I think that's all. No mistakes here, I believe.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 26 and 20 is \\boxed{520}.\n\n\nTo find the product of 26 and 20, we follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 26 by the ones place digit of 20 (which is 0):**\n   \\[\n   26 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 26 by the tens place digit of 20 (which is 2, representing 20):**\n   \\[\n   26 \\times 20 = 26 \\times 2 \\times 10 = 52 \\times 10 = 520\n   \\]\n\n3. **Sum the results of the two steps:**\n   \\[\n   0 + 520 = 520\n   \\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{520}\\).", '']
