atches.\n\nSo the correct answer should be 5429. But in my initial thought process, I messed up the numbers because I was thinking of a different problem. I need to make sure I stay focused on the actual numbers given here.\n\nTherefore, after carefully redoing the steps, the product of 89 and 61 is indeed 5429.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 89 and 61 is \\boxed{5429}.\n\n\nTo find the product of 89 and 61, we can break down the multiplication into steps using the distributive property.\n\n1. Multiply 89 by the ones place digit (1) of 61:\n   \\[\n   89 \\times 1 = 89\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 89 by the tens place digit (60) of 61:\n   \\[\n   89 \\times 60 = 5340\n   \\]\n\n3. Sum the results of the two steps:\n   \\[\n   89 + 5340 = 5429\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 89 and 61 is \\(\\boxed{5429}\\).",
