emplate format properly, following the user's example.\n\nWait, the user's example had the steps written as:\n\nFor number1 27 and number2 153 (three digits):\n\n1. Multiply 27 by 3 (ones place)\n\n2. Multiply 27 by 50 (tens place)\n\n3. Multiply 27 by 100 (hundreds place)\n\nThen sum all three.\n\nSo for the current problem, 98 and 76 (two digits):\n\n1. Multiply 98 by 6 (ones place of 76)\n\n2. Multiply 98 by 70 (tens place of 76, which is 7*10)\n\nThen sum those two.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 7448. I think that's right. I should present this in the structure the user wants.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 98 and 76?  \n# Reasoning:  \nLet's think step by step. 76 has two digits, so we can break it into two steps.  \n1. Multiply 98 by the ones place digit **6** of 76:  \n   \\(98 \\times 6 = 588\\).  \n2. Multiply 98 by the tens place digit **70** (since 7 is in the tens place):  \n   \\(98 \\times 70 = 6,\\!860\\).  \n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\(588 + 6,\\!860 = 7,\\!448\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{7448}\\).", '']
