0 is 7960, then +91 is 8051. So total is 8051.\n\nWait, but let me verify with another method. 97*83 can be computed as (100 - 3)*(80 +3). Maybe use the distributive property: 100*80 + 100*3 -3*80 -3*3. That would be 8000 + 300 -240 -9 = 8000 + 300 is 8300, minus 240 is 8060, minus 9 is 8051. Okay, same result. So that\'s correct.\n\nTherefore, following the template:\n\nThe problem is 97 * 83. Break down 83 into 3 and 80.\n\n1. Multiply 97 by 3: 291\n2. Multiply 97 by 80: 7760\nSum the two results: 291 + 7760 = 8051\n\nSo the answer should be 8051.\n\nWait, but let me check once more with standard multiplication:\n\n   97\nx 83\n-------\n  291  (97*3)\n7760   (97*80, shifted one position to the left)\n-------\n8051\n\nYes, that\'s correct. So I think that\'s the right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 97 and 83 is \\boxed{8051}.\n\n\nTo find the product of 97 and 83, we can break down the multiplication into steps based on the digits of the second number (83):\n\n1. Multiply 97 by the ones place digit (3):\n   \\[\n   97 \\times 3 = 291\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 97 by the tens place digit (80):\n   \\[\n   97 \\times 80 = 7760\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these two steps:\n\\[\n291 + 7760 = 8051\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 97 and 83 is \\(\\boxed{8051}\\).', '']
