umbers, but now it's clear. Okay, so I'll go with 2212.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 28 and 79 is \\boxed{2212}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 28 and 79, we can break down the multiplication into steps based on the digits of the second number (79):\n\n1. **Multiply 28 by the ones place digit (9):**\n   \\[\n   28 \\times 9 = 252\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(20 \\times 9 = 180\\) and \\(8 \\times 9 = 72\\), then \\(180 + 72 = 252\\).\n\n2. **Multiply 28 by the tens place digit (70):**\n   \\[\n   28 \\times 70 = 1960\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(28 \\times 7 = 196\\), then multiply by 10 to get \\(1960\\).\n\n3. **Sum the results of the two steps:**\n   \\[\n   252 + 1960 = 2212\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 28 and 79 is \\(\\boxed{2212}\\).",
