r digits of number2 if it has" (since it\'s three digits, the hundreds place was next).\n\nThen sum all the step results.\n\nSo applying that to 74×96 (which has two digits):\n\n1. Multiply 74 by 6 (ones place digit).\n\n2. Multiply 74 by 90 (tens place digit).\n\nSum them.\n\nTherefore, the reasoning should be:\n\nLet\'s think step by step. 96 has two digits, so two steps.\n\n1. Multiply 74 by the ones place digit 6 of 96: 74×6=444.\n\n2. Multiply 74 by the tens place digit 90 of 96: 74×90=6660.\n\nSum the results: 444 +6660 =7104.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 7104.\n\nI think that\'s correct. Let me confirm once more.\n\nAlternatively, using the standard multiplication:\n\n   74\n\n×96\n\n--------\n\nFirst multiply 74×6=444.\n\nThen multiply 74×90 (which is 74×9 shifted one position to the left, so 666 shifted becomes 6660).\n\nAdding those gives 444+6660=7104. Yes, correct.\n\nAlright, so the reasoning is properly structured.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 74 and 96 is \\boxed{7104}.\n\n\nTo find the product of 74 and 96, we can break down the multiplication into steps based on the digits of the second number (96).\n\n### Reasoning:\nLet\'s think step by step. 96 has two digits, so we can split the multiplication into two steps:\n1. **Multiply 74 by the ones place digit (6) of 96:**\n   \\[\n   74 \\times 6 = 444\n   \\]\n2. **Multiply 74 by the tens place digit (90) of 96:**\n   \\[\n   74 \\times 90 = 74 \\times (9 \\times 10) = (74 \\times 9) \\times 10 = 666 \\times 10 = 6660\n   \\]\n\n### Summing the results:\n\\[\n444 + 6660 = 7104\n\\]\n\n### Answer:\nThe product of 74 and 96 is \\boxed{7104}.', '']
