hich gives 6570. Then adding the two partial products (73 and 6570) gives the total. So that\'s correct.\n\nI think that\'s the correct structure. Therefore, the answer is 6643.\n\nJust to be absolutely sure, let me compute 73×91 directly:\n\n73 × 91:\n\nCompute 70×90 = 6300,\n\n70×1 = 70,\n\n3×90 =270,\n\n3×1=3,\n\nTotal: 6300 +70=6370, plus 270=6640, plus 3=6643. Yep.\n\nTherefore, the answer is correct.\n\n</think>', ''] 90%|######### | 451/500 [3:41:21<42:29, 52.03s/it]
