e final answer is 4960. I think that's solid. No mistakes in the steps now. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 80 and 62 is \\boxed{4960}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 80 and 62?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 62 has two digits, so we can break it down into two steps:\n1. Multiply 80 by the ones place digit 2 of 62:\n   \\[\n   80 \\times 2 = 160\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 80 by the tens place digit 60 of 62:\n   \\[\n   80 \\times 60 = 4800\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n160 + 4800 = 4960\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{4960}.", '']
